  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Markovnikov&rsquo;s product is formed when a stable carbocation is formed on the more substituted carbon.</p><p>In <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo></math> the carbocation formed will be destabilized by strong <math><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></math> group of <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><mo>.</mo></math> Hence, the Anti-Markovnikov&rsquo;s product will be formed.</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/188a3e1f-5572-4059-81a2-08fabeb9dd35-image.png\" style=\"width: 684px; height: 117px;\" /></p>",
